WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:19.304
looked at Jean Valjean holding out the doll to her.

2
00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:23.167
Then she ran and hid as far as she could under the table.

3
00:00:24.208 --> 00:00:26.089
No one in the room moved or spoke.

4
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.212
Only Monsieur Thenardier dared to say anything.

5
00:00:30.112 --> 00:00:34.233
"That doll must have cost at least thirty francs," he whispered to his wife.

6
00:00:34.853 --> 00:00:39.015
"This fellow obviously has money, so it's time to turn on the charm."

7
00:00:39.035 --> 00:00:43.316
"My dear Cosette," said Monsieur Thenardier.

8
00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:45.877
"This kind man has given you a present.

9
00:00:46.357 --> 00:00:48.717
Please come out and accept it."

10
00:00:49.658 --> 00:00:55.499
Cosette crawled out from under the table and gazed at the beautiful doll with both terror and hope.

11
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.301
She worried that if she touched it, the Thenardiers would scold and beat her.

12
00:01:00.841 --> 00:01:03.922
But it was so beautiful "Is it true?"

13
00:01:04.222 --> 00:01:05.182
Cosette burst out.

14
00:01:05.202 --> 00:01:06.542
"Is the doll for me?"

15
00:01:07.323 --> 00:01:10.444
For a moment Valjean could not speak for fear of weeping.

16
00:01:10.964 --> 00:01:14.345
He nodded to Cosette and put the doll's hand in hers.

17
00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:18.986
"I'll call her Catharine," said Cosette, hugging the doll.

18
00:01:19.006 --> 00:01:21.247
"May I sit her in a chair, madame?"

19
00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:26.556
"Yes, my child," said Madame Thenardier.

20
00:01:26.576 --> 00:01:30.859
Her voice was as sweet as honey, but her eyes were full of rage.

21
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.323
Cosette placed the doll on a chair, and then sat on the floor admiring it.

22
00:01:36.843 --> 00:01:38.404
"Why don't you play with your new doll?"

23
00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:39.605
asked Valjean.

24
00:01:39.625 --> 00:01:42.287
"Oh, I am playing!"

25
00:01:42.707 --> 00:01:45.249
said Cosette without taking her eyes from the doll.

26
00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.231
Valjean had to turn away and wipe his eyes.

27
00:01:49.252 --> 00:01:54.856
Madame Thenardier whispered to her husband, "It's outrageous that Cosette has such a nice doll.

28
00:01:55.316 --> 00:01:58.237
Tomorrow I'm throwing that child out on the street."

29
00:01:59.037 --> 00:02:02.318
The next morning before dawn, Valjean came into the kitchen.

30
00:02:02.338 --> 00:02:06.579
"Ah, monsieur," said Madame Thenardier.

31
00:02:06.599 --> 00:02:08.700
"Are you leaving us today?"

32
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.621
"Yes, I must be going."

33
00:02:12.361 --> 00:02:14.181
She handed him the bill for his stay.

34
00:02:14.201 --> 00:02:19.663
"I'm sorry we have to charge so much, but we're just getting by.

35
00:02:19.683 --> 00:02:23.604
I have my own girls, and then there's this other girl we've taken in."

36
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.022
Valjean did not want to betray too much interest in Cosette.

37
00:02:28.042 --> 00:02:31.284
"Suppose I were to take her off your hands?"

38
00:02:32.464 --> 00:02:35.046
Madame Thenardier could not believe her good fortune.

39
00:02:35.066 --> 00:02:38.688
"I must fetch my husband, so you can discuss it with him."

40
00:02:39.588 --> 00:02:43.790
After a whispered conversation with his wife, Monsieur Thenardier came into the room.

41
00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:47.853
"I hear you want to take our little Cosette away from us.

42
00:02:48.553 --> 00:02:51.294
I'm sorry; I cannot consent to that.

43
00:02:51.815 --> 00:02:53.656
We've grown so attached to her.

44
00:02:54.724 --> 00:02:59.587
It's true that she costs us money and she has her faults, but I can't just give her

45
00:02:59.647 --> 00:03:00.867
away to a stranger."

46
00:03:01.788 --> 00:03:07.751
Valjean looked steadily at Thenardier as the innkeeper continued to pretend that he was devoted to Cosette.

47
00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:14.495
"If you took her away," said Thenardier, "I'd want to know your name and where you live.

48
00:03:15.315 --> 00:03:20.318
Then I could come visit her, and she'd know that her good foster father was still watching over

49
00:03:20.398 --> 00:03:26.609
her." "Monsieur Thenardier, if I take Cosette, you'll never know my name or my address.

50
00:03:27.189 --> 00:03:30.171
My intention is that she'll never see you again in her lifetime.

51
00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:32.251
Do you agree to this or not?"

52
00:03:33.332 --> 00:03:34.873
The innkeeper did not respond.

53
00:03:35.513 --> 00:03:36.873
He had noticed something.

54
00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:42.716
Even before the stranger had proposed taking Cosette, the man had kept looking at her the previous night.

55
00:03:43.516 --> 00:03:46.998
Who was this man and why was he so interested in Cosette?

56
00:03:47.498 --> 00:03:51.400
He was too old to be her father, but could he be her grandfather?

57
00:03:52.308 --> 00:03:55.450
And why did he have so much money when he was dressed so poorly?

58
00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:59.112
Thenardier decided that now was the moment to act boldly.

59
00:03:59.132 --> 00:04:05.716
"Monsieur, if you want Cosette, then you must give me fifteen hundred francs."

60
00:04:07.557 --> 00:04:13.620
Valjean opened his wallet, pulled out three five-hundred-franc bills, and laid them on the table.

61
00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.141
"Bring Cosette."

62
00:04:16.081 --> 00:04:20.264
When Cosette came into the kitchen, she found Valjean untying his bundle.

63
00:04:20.896 --> 00:04:28.941
He presented her with a warm dress, apron, undergarments, petticoat, scarf, wool stockings, and shoes.

64
00:04:29.862 --> 00:04:33.144
All of the clothing was black because her mother was dead.

65
00:04:34.085 --> 00:04:38.067
As dawn broke, Valjean walked away from the Thenardiers' inn.

66
00:04:38.668 --> 00:04:44.272
He was leading a little girl in mourning clothes who was carrying a large doll dressed in pink.

67
00:04:45.012 --> 00:04:50.476
Cosette did not know the man who had taken her away from that horrid life, but she trusted

68
00:04:50.536 --> 00:04:56.495
him. She felt that she was no longer alone and that she had someone who would protect her.

69
00:04:57.455 --> 00:05:02.658
Soon after Cosette had left the inn, Thenardier showed the fifteen hundred francs to his wife.

70
00:05:02.678 --> 00:05:05.680
"You fool," she said.

71
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:10.382
"Is that all you got for the girl when that man was carrying so much money in his

72
00:05:10.462 --> 00:05:13.184
wallet?" "You're right.

73
00:05:13.804 --> 00:05:14.945
I should have asked for more.

74
00:05:15.585 --> 00:05:18.227
He probably would have given me fifteen thousand francs."

75
00:05:18.847 --> 00:05:20.628
Monsieur Thenardier put on his hat.

76
00:05:21.224 --> 00:05:22.305
"I'm going after them."

77
00:05:23.206 --> 00:05:28.069
By the time Thenardier left the inn, Valjean and Cosette had a good head start.

78
00:05:28.529 --> 00:05:34.673
But a man in pursuit walks quickly, and a child walks slowly and needs to rest often.

79
00:05:35.454 --> 00:05:39.216
Thenardier caught up to them when they were sitting by a path near some woods.

80
00:05:39.777 --> 00:05:43.499
His walk had given him just enough time to formulate a scheme.

81
00:05:43.519 --> 00:05:49.964
"Pardon me, monsieur, here are your fifteen hundred francs," Thenardier said to Valjean.

82
00:05:50.892 --> 00:05:51.532
"What do you mean?"

83
00:05:51.552 --> 00:05:54.793
"I mean that I'm taking back Cosette."

84
00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:58.755
The little girl shuddered and huddled close to Valjean.

85
00:05:58.775 --> 00:06:02.656
"You're taking back Cosette?"

86
00:06:03.056 --> 00:06:05.977
Valjean said slowly as he looked Thenardier in the eye.

87
00:06:05.997 --> 00:06:10.999
"I've thought it over, and she really belongs with her mother.

88
00:06:11.679 --> 00:06:14.040
Now you'll say that her mother is dead.

89
00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:19.122
In that case I can only give her to someone who brings me a written order from the

90
00:06:19.162 --> 00:06:22.564
mother, saying that I should deliver Cosette to him."

91
00:06:23.525 --> 00:06:28.928
Valjean reached into a pocket and produced the letter that Fantine had signed before she died.

92
00:06:28.948 --> 00:06:34.911
"You're completely correct," he said, "but I think this letter will settle the matter.

93
00:06:35.412 --> 00:06:36.952
You're familiar with the signature?"

94
00:06:37.853 --> 00:06:41.855
Thenardier read the letter and instantly recognized Fantine's signature.

95
00:06:42.536 --> 00:06:48.494
Defeated, he decided to make one last desperate attempt to get money from Valjean.

96
00:06:48.514 --> 00:06:55.075
"It says here that the bearer of this letter will pay all the money that Fantine owes me.

97
00:06:56.076 --> 00:07:00.517
It will take me a while to calculate exactly how much that is, but I know it's quite

98
00:07:00.777 --> 00:07:01.777
a large amount."

99
00:07:03.358 --> 00:07:05.799
Valjean stood up and towered over Thenardier.

100
00:07:05.819 --> 00:07:09.900
"Now you listen to me," he said in a menacing voice.

101
00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:16.162
"I know exactly how much money Fantine owed you, and I know that she paid you much more

102
00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:16.723
than that."

103
00:07:17.523 --> 00:07:19.424
But Thenardier was not intimidated.

104
00:07:19.444 --> 00:07:23.165
"I'll take Cosette back if you don't give me three thousand francs."

105
00:07:24.126 --> 00:07:26.407
Valjean said quietly, "Come, Cosette."

106
00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:31.989
He took her hand in his left hand, and picked up his walking stick with his right hand.

107
00:07:32.749 --> 00:07:38.732
Thenardier noted the enormous size of the heavy stick and decided not to say anything more.

108
00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.581
He watched as Valjean disappeared into the woods with Cosette.

109
00:07:42.601 --> 00:07:47.444
"I'm going to keep an eye on them," he decided after a few minutes.

110
00:07:48.284 --> 00:07:53.086
He had followed the pair for two or three hundred feet before Valjean turned around and glared at

111
00:07:53.146 --> 00:08:00.109
him. Valjean's look was so threatening that Thenardier decided to abandon them and go home.
